From 0ebef09fc56fc2d38386fadab9186999bf2bbec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duchil6063 <duchil6063@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 03:02:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] itasha: an Itasha menu, headless geometry dump, and
 split-at-a-line

Adds everything ForzaSqueegee needs from the editor:

* dumpItashaGeometry / --itasha-dump - project the car mesh per section
  into a depth raster, answered before QApplication so it runs headless.
* [Itasha] menu - load a design into a section (plan.json, KFPS typecode
  JSON, or a vinyl group), auto-place, grow/drop decoration, motif family,
  mirror, base paint, export to a game container, export a group. Each
  item saves the project, calls the engine named by
  QSettings("itasha/command"), and reopens what it wrote. Menu items act
  on the artwork you picked - selectedItashaGroups walks up to the nearest
  FS: group. Engine output is read as UTF-8.
* [Edit -> Split Selection at a Line] - cut the selected layers or groups
  into two groups at one line. Game shapes cannot be halved, so a layer
  the line crosses is copied into both groups; the slack widens that
  overlap inward. The line is dragged on the canvas (SplitTool) and the
  side panel holds the numbers.
